  "comparison": "Candidate service package minus diagnosis-only baseline, matched by condition, variant and seed. Only complete matched physical traces enter differences. Undefined prices are excluded separately for each monetary metric, with explicit available-pair counts. Failed/incomplete cases and all attempts remain visible.",
  "policy_tuning": "Greedy production dispatch and the existing observation-based local service rules are frozen. No tuning, training or joint service/process optimization occurs in this protocol.",
  "resolution": {
    "plant_basis": "Reference or active-run plant, production costs, sensors, process implementation choices and solar design. The protocol supplies service hardware, logistics, service prices and challenge settings; every replacement of an active-run value is recorded.",
    "variants": "Apply declared numerical scales, then replacements, then the condition; explicit tier hours, horizon, solver budget and seed apply last. No implicit capacity scaling of hardware or inventory. Named solar capacity factors also scale every section and converter of an explicit active design; converter fractions change only the converter. All resolved values are retained.",
    "arms": "Separate runs with one frozen controller policy each. Arm patches may change service machinery, thresholds and prices, but not shared plant/weather/fault inputs or the common environmental-loss model.",
    "weather": "Saved synthetic reference and forecasts. Each matched group must have identical weather bytes. Wind and rain for work eligibility are explicitly assumed, not site observations.",
    "faults": "Persistent module damage, a resettable module trip, or flow-channel bias starts at hour 10; no fault clears merely because a timer elapsed. Injected cause is unavailable to every controller.",
    "randomness": "Named sensor channels and exogenous seed are matched. Mission outcomes use their existing named draws; different missions/exposure can produce different outcomes. This is not a guarantee of identical observations across trajectories.",
    "costs": "All service assumptions are frozen; allocated period cost, action-dependent cost and modelled expenditure remain distinct. This protocol retains the version-1 comparison boundary: calendar maintenance allowance only, with executed routine maintenance and dock standby explicitly disabled. Dedicated support studies vary those assumptions.",
    "terminal": "Count the complete run including startup. Keep battery, gas, thermal state, robot energy, usable supplies, completed-unverified and unfinished work. No sale proceeds or credit for postponing work. Extended sensitivity windows expose boundary dependence."
  },
  "metric_definitions": {
    "methane_kg": "Sum of applied methane; hydrogen inventory is separate.",
    "total_eur": "Allocated plant and service period cost; undefined if an applicable price is missing.",
    "service_expenditure_eur": "Modelled service billings and procurement events; not total plant cash flow or invoices.",
    "human_work": "Site visits, actual committed crew hours and remote hours are separate.",
    "recovery": "Physical fault-active hours are retrospective truth; observation-based diagnosis and completed-unverified work remain distinct.",
    "terminal": "All ending inventories and service state retained; unfinished and completed-unverified orders reported separately."
  },
  "checks": [
    "Independent physical, service-resource and three-view economic audit for every complete arm",
    "Identical matched weather hashes and exogenous input signatures",
    "Preserved protocol, original prices, source, attempts and numerical rerun differences",
    "Explicit incomplete data, solver limitations, unsupported prices and unfinished work"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Illustrative hardware, procedure reliability, sensor models and prices; no empirical reliability or economic calibration.",
    "Three seeds provide descriptive comparisons, not population confidence intervals.",
    "Packages change sensing, action capability and support together; a result cannot attribute unique causal importance to the rover.",
    "A rover reads a prepared contact. It does not mechanically replace a module; that intervention remains human work in this protocol.",
    "Greedy production and local service rules can be outperformed by simpler hardware packages; no planner or robot superiority is required.",
    "Short recovery windows do not establish annual installation economics. No soiling removal occurs in these arms; all retain the same environmental loss.",
    "Actual scheduled-maintenance work, dock standby power and coordinated service scheduling are subsequent models. Their absence limits this edition and is frozen in its source."
  ],
  "review": {
    "status": "authored",
    "scope": "Initial matched-package recovery protocol. Covers existing service mechanisms only; later prepared-module/manipulator comparisons require a new protocol revision. Revision 3 freezes inactive explicit-cleaning/contact defaults and names capacity scaling for an active section design."
  }
}
